  "added": "2026-10-23",
  "notes": "Recalls the Elta Music Solar 42N, a stereo drone and ambient machine. Three drones of up to five detuned saws each swell in and out through their own AR envelopes, gated by three pulse generators; FX, LFO and EDIT switch them on and off, ARP the two noise voices (bursts: noise stepped by a sample & hold; bleeps: a tone whose pitch a second sample & hold of the noise steps). The keys play two voices of a morphing wavetable with a square sub and pulse-width modulation, and PLAY runs a 5-step line through them. Each side has its own distortion and 12 dB band-pass filter, swept together by an LFO and a looping envelope; a long reverb feeds a ping-pong delay."
 }
